# Wary Farmer: "At the beginning of your end step, if another creature entered the battlefield under your control this turn,
# surveil 1" (CR 603.4, 701.25). Turn 1: the Farmer is the only creature that entered (an Island entered too, which is no
# creature), and "another" leaves it out, so its end step passes with no surveil (the library keeps its 8 cards). Turn 3: an
# Ornithopter entering is another creature, so at the end step Bot1 looks at exactly one card, the top Counterspell, and puts
# it into the graveyard; Lightning Bolt is the next card and stays (surveil 1 looks at one card, not two); the turn 3 draw
# took the Mountain.

